From: Jaydeep <106300970+jaydeeppatel1111@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 07:24:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ROCM-24764 - guard Thread::Release() against null virtualDevice_ (#6197)

When hsa_queue_create() fails (e.g. KFD hardware queue slots exhausted
under high process concurrency), createVirtualDevice() returns nullptr,
leaving Thread::virtualDevice_ as null. In the AMD_DIRECT_DISPATCH path,
HostQueue::terminate() calls thread_.Release() unconditionally, causing
a null pointer dereference.

Add a null check in Thread::Release() to handle this gracefully.

(cherry picked from ROCm/clr commit 7d979ab5a0aadbc9bc3a99f2411bb06b5ca2c9e2)
[Artur Andrzejczak: backported to the rocclr 7.1.1 source. The same crash was
 reached on a BC-250 (gfx1013) from the KFD resident-memory limit rather than
 from queue-slot exhaustion, through hipGraphInstantiate creating the null
 stream; found and analysed with Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic) before the
 upstream commit was known, and replaced by it once it was.]
Link: https://github.com/ROCm/clr/commit/7d979ab5a0aadbc9bc3a99f2411bb06b5ca2c9e2
Signed-off-by: Artur Andrzejczak <andrzejczak.artur@gmail.com>
---
--- a/rocclr/platform/commandqueue.hpp
+++ b/rocclr/platform/commandqueue.hpp
@@ -184,7 +184,11 @@
       }
     }
 
-    void Release() const { virtualDevice_->release(); }
+    void Release() const {
+      if (virtualDevice_ != nullptr) {
+        virtualDevice_->release();
+      }
+    }
 
     //! Get virtual device for the current thread
     device::VirtualDevice* vdev() const { return virtualDevice_; }
